			<div class="content" id="post-content-1675418">
									

<p>Eh, I'm okay with this being PL.</p>
<p>The Factory can force a uniform behavior through supernatural means. Wondertainment can either do the same, or is a single person in the first place. But PL was a human organization. It had branches. We don't know how independent those branches were. There are amoral or misguided people everywhere, especially in the Foundationverse. I would be more surprised if nothing like this ever happened to them.</p>
<p>Also, the cruel part is debatable. If these homunculi are indeed not sentient, then what was done not only wasn't cruel, but was even preferable to animal testing. You can argue that the personnel's behavior was caused by human tendency to anthropomorphise non-living object, and when that object looks like a human, especially someone they knew, it becomes increasingly hard to remain detached.</p>
<p>Well, they killed five humans to create the homunculi. That was ethically not good. But the process is presumably painless, and five people is not that big of a death toll. The rest is in the grey area.</p>

