														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1675576">
									

<p>I look at it as I do animal testing. I'm certain PL was doing animal testing, and anything done to non-sentient clones wouldn't really be any different than &quot;regular&quot; animal testing.</p>
<p>The thing I find stretching how I view PL is that the originals die while being cloned. That seems unnecessarily grimdark. (Also, the originals dieing combined with &quot;take your daughter to work day&quot; makes it&#8230; a bit lolprometheus.)</p>
<p>Especially when the person living through the copying is actually even more horrific. I mean, it's one thing to watch something that looks human get killed repeatedly. Now imagine a long day of dealing with that, and going home to look the original in the eye. (or perhaps the horror of being the original and watching yourself asking to be disposed of.)</p>
<p>If that one bit could be dropped, I think it'd make it match PL a lot better.</p>

							</div>

								
					
